From 8535c193bc78f16858fd39ae92b8ea2c40d70279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 07:29:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: the WAN page's UPnP toggle wrote neither enable key

197d3b8321 made the READ side derive both gates from one helper. This is the
write side. validate_apply() propagates a posted wan_<name> to wan<N>_<name>
only once it has seen wan_unit and only if the closed validate_apply_input_value()
accepts it - and the WAN page posts the UNINDEXED wan_upnp_enable only, so the
generic upnp_enable had NO WRITER on this path at all. That half is proven from
source and is what this fixes.

An explicit wan_upnp_enable branch now sits ahead of the generic propagation. It
resolves the unit from wan_primary_ifunit() when wan_unit is absent, validates
the value as a boolean itself, and writes wan<N>_upnp_enable and upnp_enable in
lockstep, so the pair cannot drift back apart through the GUI.

Eliminated while reading the apply loop, recorded so they are not re-chased: the
loop iterates router_defaults and pulls by name, so field order in the form is
irrelevant (wan_unit at defaults.c:2494 precedes wan_upnp_enable at 2603);
nvram_check() rejects only on over-length, so a 1-char boolean passes; and the
radios ARE enabled for dhcp/pppoe/static/bridge by fixed_change_wan_proto_type().
That leaves validate_apply_input_value() as the only unexplained gate, and this
branch does not depend on it either way. Which gate actually blocked on metal is
still unproven - toggle UPnP after the flash and confirm both keys flip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/web.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
index d08220224a..1608d1a130 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
@@ -4538,6 +4538,36 @@ int validate_apply(webs_t wp, json_object *root)
 #endif
 				}
 			}
+			/* UPnP is gated by two nvram keys: the per-unit wan<N>_upnp_enable that
+			 * miniupnpd and the firewall builders read, and the generic upnp_enable
+			 * that older callers and pages still consult. The WAN page posts the
+			 * unindexed wan_upnp_enable, so the generic key was never written here at
+			 * all and the two could drift apart - a box could list UPnP mappings while
+			 * nothing was ever DNATed, or run the jump with no daemon behind it.
+			 * Write both in lockstep. The value is a plain boolean, so it is validated
+			 * here rather than through the generic wan_ path. */
+			else if(!strcmp(name, "wan_upnp_enable")) {
+				int upnp_unit = (unit != -1) ? unit : wan_primary_ifunit();
+
+				if(strcmp(value, "0") && strcmp(value, "1")) {
+					dbg("validate(wan) %s=%s is not boolean\n", name, value);
+					continue;
+				}
+
+				snprintf(prefix, sizeof(prefix), "wan%d_", upnp_unit);
+				(void)strlcat_r(prefix, "upnp_enable", tmp, sizeof(tmp));
+
+				if(strcmp(nvram_safe_get(tmp), value)) {
+					nvram_set(tmp, value);
+					nvram_modified = 1;
+					_dprintf("wan_ set %s=%s\n", tmp, value);
+				}
+				if(strcmp(nvram_safe_get("upnp_enable"), value)) {
+					nvram_set("upnp_enable", value);
+					nvram_modified = 1;
+					_dprintf("wan_ set upnp_enable=%s\n", value);
+				}
+			}
 			else if(!strncmp(name, "wan_", 4) && unit != -1 && strcmp(name, "wan_ifname_x")) {
 				snprintf(prefix, sizeof(prefix), "wan%d_", unit);
 				(void)strlcat_r(prefix, name+4, tmp, sizeof(tmp));
-- 
